# A ledger stamp is the SHA-256 of the specification's bytes. Git's automatic
# line-ending conversion rewrites those bytes on checkout, so a Windows working
# tree would report every stamp MISMATCH against a file nobody edited.
#
# Turn conversion off for everything. Files stay exactly as committed, on both
# platforms, and a stamp means what it says.
* -text

# Shell scripts need LF whatever an editor does to them.
*.sh text eol=lf
